## What the map asked

E1's bank cap, and it bound through a mechanism I had to correct myself about mid-ride. `Economy` **refuses the credit** once gold sits at the 200 cap — so a full purse doesn't waste surplus, it switches panning off. That makes spending an income mechanic. The run panned 720 and never let the purse pin.

## Two things worth flagging

**My own notebook was wrong about this map.** Generation 2 recorded "w10/680g" here, and I planned the first half of this heat on that reading — that outcome `gold` was cumulative earnings, so spending was free. It isn't: `gold` is the banked purse, 680 is impossible against a 200 cap, and 720/76 is what this engine actually produces. The map's geometry, secure wave and cap all reproduced exactly; only my number was bad.

**The ranked margin is thinner than the play.** With waves pinned at 10 and time pinned at 300s by a fixed-wave secure, gold is the *only* free ranking axis — and my controller was tuned to keep the purse moving, which is right for throughput and wrong for the scoreboard. A line that stops buying two waves out and lets ~2.4 g/s refill to the cap should bank 200+ on the same ride. I only had that read after the securing run, and the stop rule correctly ends the heat at the first secure rather than letting me chase it.

The play itself had wide margin in every other direction: hero never below its running maximum, finishing 175/175 at level 15; one of twelve works wrecked, at t=287 of 300; threats peaked at 23 against a 60 cap.
